# The mouse, written by hand. With mighty=1 the "press a key" pauses and most menus wait in
# Mickey (place 3), which a mouse button also ends; every wait this script clicks at is one. Each click is a press and a release given at once,
# so it also checks that Mickey does not lose a click whose release comes before it reads the
# buttons. The earlier Mickey (MICKEY.BM, which read only the buttons' last state) failed this
# script in 3 of 6 runs (2026-11-05).
#   - "press a key or mouse button": a left click;
#   - the title menu: Start NEW Game, clicked (menu, switch 11);
#   - Start Year: 1939, clicked;
#   - the briefing: a right click;
#   - the main menu: Paris clicked on the map, then Reims, which moves Elite Unit 5 there;
#   - END TURN clicked in the main menu, then a right click (Esc) at its Yes / NOT YET.
# It then quits with keys, which Mickey also takes: Files, Quit, Yes.
#! seed 1939
#! cfg mighty=1

# The pause before the title menu.
prompt
digest
mouse 100 100
press 1
release 1

# The title menu: Start NEW Game.
prompt
digest
mouse 60 263
press 1
release 1

# Start Year: 1939.
prompt
digest
mouse 165 199
press 1
release 1

# The briefing.
prompt
digest
press 2
release 2

# The main menu: Paris (city 40, at 111, 127), then Reims (city 42, at 144, 126).
prompt
digest
mouse 112 128
press 1
release 1
prompt
digest
mouse 143 125
press 1
release 1

# END TURN, then a right click at Yes / NOT YET.
prompt
digest
mouse 565 295
press 1
release 1
prompt
digest
press 2
release 2

# Files, Quit, then Yes by its letter, and a key for END's "Press any key to continue".
prompt
digest
text f
prompt
text q
prompt
digest
text y
repeat space
